WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.260
The first NPC you meet,

00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:03.160
in the Ringed City DLC,

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:04.600
is an old Pilgrim woman

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:07.100
who casts her gaze over the Dreg Heap.

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:09.640
she talks about how she feels like a god,

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:11.760
looking over this grand sight

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:13.680
of kingdoms and townships

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:15.000
come together.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:17.760
She then goes on to say;

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:18.980
"Far below,

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:22.220
there's a deep, dark hole carved out of a tree".

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:24.640
From time to time, voices brim

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:26.280
in the depths of the cavity,

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:27.360
even now".

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:31.000
"Mutterings of the very demon that Prince Lorian spoke of,

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:32.020
I'm sure".

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:33.420
"Horrible sounds,

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:35.020
of an afflicted thing

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:36.720
yet cursing men".

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:38.340
And if you remember,

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:41.420
The Demon Prince was said to have been slain

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:42.390
by Prince Lorian,

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:45.600
eternally scorching his greatsword with fire.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:47.080
Turns out

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:48.640
he didn't finish the job,

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:50.480
and to finish it for him,

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:51.980
we have to go down.

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:54.480
The first thing that you encounter on your way down

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:55.180
are these

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:55.940
so-called,

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:56.840
Murkmen.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:01.140
You can find, and use their hand scythes and their staffs,

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:04.280
and some are even possessed by Soul Dregs,

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:04.780
which

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.860
are said to have a grave likeness

00:01:06.869 --> 00:01:08.069
to the human form.

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:12.899
And it makes sense that these creatures

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:14.660
of the deep would be down here,

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:15.380
of course,

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:18.000
because Human Dregs are supposed to

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:20.900
sink to the lowest depths imaginable,

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.360
and the entire theme of this DLC appears to be

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:25.320
descent.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:27.220
Descent down to that Demon Prince

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:28.780
the old woman mentions,

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:29.560
and

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:30.880
down to the Ringed City,

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:32.280
even beyond that.

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:33.200
But to get there,

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:34.500
you're going to have to go

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:36.100
past these angels,

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:37.000
who,

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:39.720
I reckon, are going to be responsible for most of your

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:41.200
deaths in the DLC.

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:47.680
In the room I was playing this DLC,

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:50.080
everywhere I looked around the rooms,

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:52.100
someone was dying to one of these angels.

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:54.020
They're utterly relentless,

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:54.920
and

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:56.020
especially so in

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:58.840
the second section of this area which, unfortunately,

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:01.400
isn't shown in the footage that your seeing,

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:03.060
and I think it's the best area.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:06.320
The second section is named Earthen Peak,

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:07.980
confirming theories that the

00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:09.880
windmills we saw in the previous trailer,

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:11.320
were from there.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:12.640
I can also confirm,

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:14.600
it includes a poison swamp,

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:15.840
Lothric Theives,

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:17.360
the poisonous bug things,

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:17.860
and

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.060
a female desert pyromancer,

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:21.180
and of course,

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:22.060
an angel.

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:23.360
Here though,

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:25.560
the angel makes this entire stage

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:27.800
into this huge stealth section.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:30.680
It's kind of like the Dragon God, in Demon's Souls,

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:31.540
if you played that,

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:33.060
where you have to hide,

00:02:33.069 --> 00:02:35.200
and you have to wait for it's attention to

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:35.700
wander

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:37.490
before you can continue.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:39.420
So you run from cover to cover,

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:41.500
avoiding this angel's glare,

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:44.280
and hoping it gets distracted by another enemy

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:45.880
and starts shooting them instead.

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:47.120
Really fun.

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:48.820
There's never really been a stealth

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:51.300
component to this extent in Souls,

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:52.940
and I didn't like it

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:54.540
until I decided to be

00:02:54.549 --> 00:02:55.649
really really patient,

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:56.540
and

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:57.040
then

00:02:57.420 --> 00:02:58.960
it paid off, I progressed,

00:02:58.960 --> 00:02:59.460
and

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:00.440
I figured it out,

00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:01.520
so...

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:02.260
Interestingly,

00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:02.880
uh...

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:04.440
those bolts of light that

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.190
the angel is shooting at you;

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:09.500
if you look closely it actually disperses into feathers,

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:11.580
white feathers that are akin

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:14.250
to those that you see in the Lothric royal bloodline.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.440
We talk about that in this video,

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:19.420
so that's definitely significant, from a lore point of view.

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:20.320
And

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:21.160
additionally,

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:22.299
and I'm not going to

00:03:22.299 --> 00:03:23.399
give too much away here,

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:27.180
but these angels are linked to The Pilgrims of Londor,

00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:28.360
which

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:30.840
raises some serious lore implications.

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:33.300
So it might take you a little while to get

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:36.489
past Earthen Peak and find the first boss.

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:39.000
But when you do find it, it's probably

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:40.959
going to take you even longer to beat it

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:43.060
because this fight really was quite tough.

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:45.600
No one else, I could see, could beat it.

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:46.440
And

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:48.640
I only beat it because I left the DLC,

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:50.560
I speedran to Rosaria,

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:52.080
and I respec'd my character

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:53.820
to get rid of all its faith points,

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:54.320
and

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:55.620
put it all into vigor.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:58.020
My character was soul level 125,

00:03:58.480 --> 00:03:59.440
which is really high.

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:01.540
This stuff is endgame content for sure.

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:03.320
This fight has three phases.

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:05.840
So first you fight a Crimson Bat,

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:06.960
which is a simple

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:07.760
single bat,

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.780
that teaches you the boss's moveset.

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:10.520
And then,

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:13.080
when you get The Crimson Bat to fifty percent health,

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:15.980
it summons a second boss called

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:17.620
The Demon from Below.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:21.400
And The Demon from Below looks virtually identical to

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:22.540
The Crimson Bat,

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:25.900
except that its fire is more purple than red

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:27.760
So The Demon from Below will get in

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:28.760
your face, and

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:31.080
the weak Crimson Bat will back off,

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:31.740
and

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:34.900
it mostly spams this ranged explosion attack that

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:35.720
you can see here.

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:37.580
So this is phase two,

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:39.000
and in phase two,

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:40.720
you obviously have a choice of which

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:42.020
bat to kill first.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:42.800
And

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:43.360
I think,

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:44.340
whichever one you kill,

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:46.660
affects the third phase of the fight.

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:47.800
So

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:51.180
if you kill the weakened Crimson Bat first,

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:52.960
then The Demon from Below

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:55.200
will turn into The Demon Prince,

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:59.040
who summons these floating chaos orbs that spam long-range

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:00.120
fireballs at you

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:01.140
throughout the fight.

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:02.360
However,

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:04.560
if you kill the full health

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:07.300
Demon from Below first, in phase two,

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:10.120
then The Crimson Bat will turn into The Demon

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:11.280
Prince as well,

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:12.200
except,

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:13.920
instead of the chaos orbs,

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:15.340
this Demon Prince

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:19.020
has the long-ranged laser beam you see in the footage here.

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:19.960
And,

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:20.860
in my opinion,

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:25.020
the laser beam is way easier to deal with than the orbs.

00:05:25.419 --> 00:05:27.719
It actually leaves him open a majority of the time.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:28.500
And,

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:31.980
it's a way for the developers to make phase three easier on you

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:34.320
to reward you for killing the full

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:36.290
health demon in phase two,

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:39.550
as opposed to the weakened demon in phase two.

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:41.540
I hope that makes sense,

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:42.520
but

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:43.140
regardless

00:05:43.260 --> 00:05:44.080
of what you choose,

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:46.080
when The Demon Prince is dead,

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:48.360
you get The Soul of a Demon Prince,

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:49.540
and it reads;

00:05:50.060 --> 00:05:50.940
"The Demon Prince,

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:52.840
after his defeat to Lorian,

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:54.720
retreated beneath the earth

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:58.180
and lost the memory of the flame that burned within him,

00:05:58.740 --> 00:06:00.580
marking the end of demonkind".

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:02.160
And further on,

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:05.040
we find a small envoy banner,

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:08.760
and it's just like the little ringed banner you get from Emma

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:10.500
after you kill Vordt.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:11.660
It reads;

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:16.240
"This small banner was used by envoys of Great Lord Gwyn

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:17.560
in days of yore.

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:19.520
Face the ringed cliff

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:21.100
and hold banner high

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:23.660
to summon facilitators of transport.

00:06:24.420 --> 00:06:25.440
For the pygmies,

00:06:25.640 --> 00:06:26.940
who took the dark soul,

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:29.780
the Great Lord gifted the Ringed City,

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:32.360
an isolated place at world's end,

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:33.280
and

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:35.820
he gifted his beloved youngest daughter,

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:38.380
promising her that he would come for her

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:39.600
when the day came".

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:40.700
So,

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:41.840
the dark soul,

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:44.140
surely that's what lies deep below

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:45.400
in the Ringed City.

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:46.720
And surely,

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:47.920
that's our goal

00:06:48.320 --> 00:06:50.320
And it's also the goal of others,

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:50.940
I found:

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:52.660
the Herald Knights,

00:06:52.820 --> 00:06:55.320
who became these bloated abyss creatures.

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:58.020
According to their weaponry and their armor,

00:06:58.460 --> 00:07:00.620
they also sought the dark soul,

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:03.740
but they sank into the dark with the rest of their legion:

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:05.460
their gear becoming

00:07:05.640 --> 00:07:06.300
corroded

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:08.340
and their forms becoming all

00:07:08.540 --> 00:07:09.040
bloated.

00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:10.240
And there's another

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:11.020
I can think of

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:12.680
who seeks the dark soul:

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:13.460
Gael.

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:15.460
Now, he was featured in some of the

00:07:15.460 --> 00:07:16.500
promotional material

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:17.280
and

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:18.060
now

00:07:18.220 --> 00:07:19.740
we know that's no coincidence.

00:07:20.110 --> 00:07:22.180
Hell, you can even summon him for this

00:07:22.180 --> 00:07:22.940
boss fight.

00:07:23.020 --> 00:07:23.520
And

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:25.060
you know what else I found

00:07:25.260 --> 00:07:27.160
in the middle of The Earthen Peak swamp?

00:07:28.060 --> 00:07:29.280
I found a loincloth

00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:30.240
that looks

00:07:30.460 --> 00:07:31.280
identical

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:33.160
to the one that Gael wears.

00:07:33.560 --> 00:07:34.060
So,

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:34.880
somewhere,

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:36.520
without undergarments,

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:40.220
Gael is travelling towards the dark soul with us,

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:41.000
I think.

00:07:41.240 --> 00:07:41.740
So,

00:07:41.740 --> 00:07:42.240
huh

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:42.740
that's

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:44.840
pretty significant from a lore point of view.

00:07:45.260 --> 00:07:45.760
And

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:47.800
I'm not gonna talk about that here, I'm going to talk

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:49.080
about it in my notes that

00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:49.580
are

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:51.600
below this video in the description,

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:54.020
because there is a ton of stuff that I have

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:55.000
Intentionally

00:07:55.420 --> 00:07:56.580
left out of this video,

00:07:56.900 --> 00:07:57.400
um...

00:07:57.620 --> 00:07:59.020
and you can read all those notes in the

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:00.000
description instead.

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:01.620
I'll explain why in a minute.

00:08:02.060 --> 00:08:02.980
But in those notes,

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:03.700
uh...

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:04.440
you can read about

00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:04.940
how

00:08:05.140 --> 00:08:06.260
I met the character

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:06.920
Lapp,

00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:09.200
who is an amnesiac knight

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:10.920
who has forgotten who he is,

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:13.220
and he's looking for the purging monument

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:14.840
to cure his hollowing.

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:16.940
I wrote down all of his dialogue

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:19.620
and I wrote down all of the dialogue for the

00:08:19.630 --> 00:08:22.090
Pilgrim lady at the start of the DLC.

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:23.700
Thank god I can touch-type,

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:25.080
it's so hard to keep up.

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:26.240
Uhm...

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:28.140
There's also a list of all the weapons I found,

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:30.200
including a pyromancy

00:08:30.520 --> 00:08:31.480
melee attack

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:33.320
that slaps people around with a

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:34.960
giant fan of fire.

00:08:35.440 --> 00:08:36.540
And I've also included

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:37.320
the secret

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:38.840
to killing the angels,

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:39.580
so,

00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:40.520
spoiler alert.

00:08:40.960 --> 00:08:42.760
And I've also written down what I think that could

00:08:42.760 --> 00:08:43.980
mean for the story.

00:08:44.340 --> 00:08:46.180
And I've written down a lot more.

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:48.180
And I would talk about this stuff,

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:50.500
but I hate making videos that

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:51.080
just

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:53.500
show the same footage over and over again,

00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:54.060
and

00:08:54.420 --> 00:08:55.500
this is the only footage I have

00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:57.160
and this stuff is really interesting and

00:08:57.160 --> 00:08:58.510
I don't really want to talk about it

00:08:58.510 --> 00:09:00.610
behind this same loop that you've been

00:09:00.610 --> 00:09:01.500
watching for like

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:02.120
what

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:02.760
10 minutes now?

00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:05.400
So I think this is the best way to get it

00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:06.080
across to you.

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:06.860
But uhm...

00:09:06.860 --> 00:09:08.160
these are the kind of notes I make

